FILED s533c (Opus, 2026-11-04), found by the family probes of the structured `local` (scratch/s533c/p/b1.pl), PRE-EXISTING (main 0f2db817 prints the same).

REPRODUCER:
  our @a = (1, 2);
  for my $i (1 .. 2) { local $a[0] = $i; print "@a\n" }
  for my $i (5, 6) { local $a[0] = $i; print "@a\n" }
perl 5.40.3: 1 2 / 2 2 / 5 2 / 6 2
PCL (0f2db817): SCALAR(0x1) 2 / SCALAR(0x2) 2 / SCALAR(0x3) 2 / SCALAR(0x4) 2  (SILENT WRONG)
A `my $j = 7` value is right; the hash twin `local $h{k} = $i` is right.

MECHANISM: %p-local-array-elem-init-plain installed `(make-p-box INIT)`; a foreach loop variable is a BOX (an alias), so the element became a box holding a box, which stringifies as a scalar reference.  The hash twin %p-lhe-init already goes through `box-set` ("init-val goes through box-set (not raw make-p-box)").

FIX (s533c): the array macro installs a fresh box filled through box-set, the hash twin's rule.  Guard: Pl/t/local-stmt-01.t.
